-- Source module: Solutions.J6SegILSlab2
/-!
# B-line IL, B1 (streaming slab pass) §2: registers, lanes, the unit loops

**Register convention** (fixed stacks, all below `56`, none `0`; the caller's data elsewhere is
preserved, since every scratch stack is restored):

| stack | role |
|---|---|
| `rK1 = 41`, `rK2 = 42` | constants of the item programs (inputs, preserved) |
| `0` | lane 1 input (the stream; the rest `l` below it is kept), and the output |
| `rZ = 53` | lane 2 input (the second array of the zipped output pass) |
| `rT = 50`, `rT2 = 51` | lane temps (scratch) |
| `rC = 45` | the control list `flatC cs` (input, preserved) |
| `rCU = 47`, `rOP = 48`, `rARG = 49`, `rACC = 52` | scratch: used commands, current command, output |
| `rNB = 37`, `rNC = 38`, `rM = 39`, `rTOT = 40` | inputs (one value each, preserved): `pre`, `|cs|`, `m`, the output length |
| `43, 46, 54` | scratch of the item programs (§5) |
| `34, 35, 36` | the `rptX` counters (`lA lC lD`) |

`55` (`ARGM`) is the multiplication argument stack. A *lane layout* `lin inp tmp G` puts the
remaining input units `inp` and the moved units `tmp` on the lane stacks over the managed state
`G`; `LaneOK lin` says it leaves the skeleton registers alone. The unit programs (`rd`, `bk`, `dr`,
`it`) are abstract with their specifications (`RdOK`, `BkOK`, `DrOK`, `ItOK`).

Here: the managed-state op lemmas, `cf3_encK` (the `rptX` counters over a managed state), and the
loops over one slab: `dropL_runs` (drop `m` units), `zeroL_runs` (emit `m` zeros), `copyL_runs`
(move `m` units to the temps while emitting `g a u`), `backL_runs` (move them back).
-/

